  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary sight.\nEach step echoed on the pavement’s face,\nIn this urban sea, he found no place.\n\nLike ghosts they passed, with eyes cast down,\nLost in their own, private town.\nNo glance was given, no word was spoke,\nIn the city’s cold and concrete choke.\n\nAmidst the crowd, so vast and deep,\nHe felt the weight of solitude’s sleep.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
